            <h3>Terminals at Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta</h3>
            <p>Atlanta operates two massive terminal complexes - Domestic and International - connected by the Plane Train automated people mover. </p>
            <h3>Domestic Terminal (North and South) </h3>
            <p>Handles all domestic carriers and most domestic departures. </p>
            <h4>Facilities: </h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Comprehensive check-in halls for all major airlines</li>
                <li>Security screening with TSA PreCheck and CLEAR lanes</li>
                <li>Extensive retail and dining options</li>
                <li>Ground transportation center</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Concourse T through F</h3>
            <p>Seven concourses radiating from the central terminal, connected by the Plane Train and pedestrian walkways. </p>
            <h4>Features by concourse: </h4>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Concourse T:</b> Delta domestic hub operations</li>
                <li><b>Concourses A through D:</b> Primary Delta domestic and some partner operations</li>
                <li><b>Concourse E:</b> International departures and arrivals; Delta's international hub</li>
                <li><b>Concourse F:</b> International carriers and Delta's premium check-in</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Rome-bound passengers on Delta's seasonal nonstop or connecting through European hubs typically depart from Concourses E or F. </p>
            <h3>Transportation to Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta</h3>
            <h4>MARTA Rail</h4>
            <p>The Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority's Red and Gold lines provide direct rail service from downtown Atlanta and other metro locations. </p>
            <h5>Benefits: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li>Most affordable option at approximately $2.50</li>
                <li>Direct connection to the airport's domestic terminal</li>
                <li>Avoids notorious Atlanta highway congestion</li>
                <li>Journey time from downtown: approximately 20 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Taxi and Rideshare</h4>
            <p>Uber, Lyft, and traditional taxis serve all terminals. </p>
            <h5>Travel times: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Off-peak:</b> 15-25 minutes from downtown</li>
                <li><b>Rush hour:</b> 30-60 minutes or longer</li>
                <li><b>Cost:</b> $25-$45 depending on destination and demand</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Driving and Parking</h4>
            <h5>Atlanta offers extensive parking: </h5>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Daily/Short-Term:</b> Adjacent to terminals at premium rates</li>
                <li><b>Economy:</b> Remote lots with shuttle service</li>
                <li><b>Park-Ride:</b> Off-airport options with frequent shuttles</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Lounges at Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Delta Sky Club (Multiple concourses)</b> - Extensive network for Medallion members and eligible cardholders</li>
                <li><b>United Club (Concourse T)</b> - For United Club members and Star Alliance Gold</li>
                <li><b>American Admirals Club (Concourse T)</b> - For Admirals Club members and oneworld Sapphire/Emerald</li>
                <li><b>The Club at ATL (Concourse F)</b> - Priority Pass accessible</li>
                <li><b>Minute Suites (Concourse B)</b> - Private rest spaces available by the hour</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Arrival Airport: Rome Fiumicino Leonardo da Vinci Airport (FCO) </h3>
            <p>Italy's largest airport honors the Renaissance polymath Leonardo da Vinci and serves as the primary gateway for visitors to Rome and central Italy. Recent terminal expansions have significantly improved the passenger experience. </p>
